group: Oh
formula: CrC6O6
construction: a metal and its donor atoms
headline: 
note: Energies in Hartree.  Molecular levels are the calculation's own orbital energies in Hartree. Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, kept in the atom's own shell order; its free-atom energy is given beside it.  Each ligand contributes one sigma donor orbital, as a ligand field diagram does; the ligands' own internal orbitals are not drawn.  Lowest empty orbital: 9A1g* (Cr 4s, 0.071 Ha). Orbital energies are not excitation energies: Δ here is not the spectroscopic ligand-field splitting.
